00:51:59,800 --> 00:52:02,800
DENR Undersecretary Analiza Rebuelta-Teh: Approximately 53.6 million, Mr. Chair.

995
00:52:02,800 --> 00:52:19,960
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: 53.6 billion po. Paano naman po nasisiguro ng DNR na ang pondo ay ginagamit para protektahan ang karapatan ng mga communities at LGUs na dapat konsultahin bago ang renewal o extension ng mga kasunduan?

996
00:52:23,080 --> 00:52:23,640
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: May answer?

997
00:52:24,040 --> 00:52:27,800
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: May I defer to MGB? Director Larry Heradez, please.

998
00:52:28,040 --> 00:52:30,300
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Director, please respond.

999
00:52:35,460 --> 00:52:47,060
MGB Director Larry M. Heradez: Meron po tayong mga programa ngayon sa DENR-MGB na tulungan yung mga small-scale miners, including po yung mga unregistered small-scale miners.

1000
00:52:47,400 --> 00:52:56,940
MGB Director Larry M. Heradez: Ang isang proyekto po na inumpisan po ng DNR, yung pong pagbibigay po ng interim small-scale miners.

1001
00:52:56,940 --> 00:52:58,200
MGB Director Larry M. Heradez: At

1002
00:52:58,200 --> 00:53:09,260
MGB Director Larry M. Heradez: hikayatin yung mga illegal miners to register and as well as to capacitate and train them to the proper ways of mining and processing of mineral ore.

1003
00:53:09,420 --> 00:53:18,200
MGB Director Larry M. Heradez: Yun po yung ating ginagawa ngayon. Aside from the usual monitoring po ng small and large-scale mining operations po sa buong bansa po.

1004
00:53:19,340 --> 00:53:20,780
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Thank you. Representative?

1005
00:53:21,220 --> 00:53:22,240
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Yes, Mr. Chair.

1006
00:53:22,420 --> 00:53:24,920
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Kaugnay po ng naunang katanungan ko.

1007
00:53:25,060 --> 00:53:28,160
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Gusto ko lang po i-raise ang mga kongkretong kaso.

1008
00:53:28,160 --> 00:53:29,660
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Patungkol sa FTAA.

1009
00:53:29,660 --> 00:53:34,960
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Nabanggit po kasi kanina na tinutulungan yung mga small-scale miners.

1010
00:53:34,960 --> 00:53:39,960
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Pero paano naman po yung mga community na merong kaso o merong problema?

1011
00:53:39,960 --> 00:53:52,260
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Sa Didipio, Nueva Vizcaya, nirenew ng gobyerno ang FTAA No. 001 kahit walang consultation at prior consent mula sa communities at LGUs.

1012
00:53:52,260 --> 00:53:57,860
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Gaya ng requirements sa local government code at EIS system.

1013
00:53:57,860 --> 00:54:00,700
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Bakit po ito napayagan ng DNR?

1014
00:54:00,760 --> 00:54:03,920
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Pwede po bang i-explain ito dito sa committee?

1015
00:54:04,220 --> 00:54:07,520
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Why this is not a violation of your mandate?

1016
00:54:07,920 --> 00:54:08,460
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Secretary?

1017
00:54:10,020 --> 00:54:11,980
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Director, this will answer that.

1018
00:54:14,420 --> 00:54:22,940
MGB Director Larry M. Heradez: Mr. Chairman, yung pong tinutukoy ng FTAA yung pong sa Oceana Gold po kung di po ako nagkakamali.

1019
00:54:22,940 --> 00:54:25,720
MGB Director Larry M. Heradez: Yung pong Oceana Gold when it was...

1020
00:54:25,720 --> 00:54:33,480
MGB Director Larry M. Heradez: nag-expired na po siya, yung pong renewal niya ay umakyat pa po sa Office of the President.

1021
00:54:33,820 --> 00:54:46,240
MGB Director Larry M. Heradez: And it has gone through various process of securing po yung particularly yung FPIC including yung social acceptability requirement.

1022
00:54:46,240 --> 00:54:56,560
MGB Director Larry M. Heradez: Kung meron po ngayon mga statement na the company is operating without public acceptability,

1023
00:54:56,560 --> 00:54:58,320
MGB Director Larry M. Heradez: ay handa po naman.

1024
00:54:58,320 --> 00:55:12,860
MGB Director Larry M. Heradez: Ang MGB na imbestigahan po yung mga allegations or yung mga facts na yun kung ito po ay may basihan na wala talagang nakuha yung mining company na social acceptability requirement.

1025
00:55:13,180 --> 00:55:25,400
MGB Director Larry M. Heradez: Pero yung pong sinasabi ko lang po, yung pong FTAA actually has gone the first term of its 25 years and is working, it is now operating under the second term.

1026
00:55:25,400 --> 00:55:28,200
MGB Director Larry M. Heradez: And wala po kami ng mga...

1027
00:55:28,200 --> 00:55:37,400
MGB Director Larry M. Heradez: na-receive na report na merong mga abuses na ginagawa ng mining company.

1028
00:55:37,600 --> 00:55:45,920
MGB Director Larry M. Heradez: But we will be ready to investigate po yung mga issues na non-acceptability ng community doon sa mining operation po.

1029
00:55:46,140 --> 00:55:52,640
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Mr. Chair, ang malas ko siguro no dahil ako yung naka-receive ng report about this.

1030
00:55:52,640 --> 00:55:55,580
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: But ito na lang po ang hilingin ko sa DNR.

1031
00:55:55,780 --> 00:55:58,580
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Pwede po ba yung DENR makapagbigay

1032
00:55:58,580 --> 00:56:09,440
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: sa atin ng data na nagpapatunay na kumpleto po sila ng requirements at hindi po sila lumabag doon or nagkaroon ng violation sa kanilang mandate.

1033
00:56:09,840 --> 00:56:22,840
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Pangalawang kaso po, ganoon din po sa Tampakan, South Cotabato, kung saan nirenew at in-extend pa ang 18 years na FTAA No. 002 ng DENR at MGB,

1034
00:56:23,860 --> 00:56:29,420
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: muli ring walang consultation at prior consent mula sa communities at LGUs.

1035
00:56:29,680 --> 00:56:40,340
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Ano po kaya ang accountability mechanisms ng DNR para sa ganitong mga renewal na lumalabag sa participatory requirements ng batas, especially sa IPRA?

1036
00:56:41,960 --> 00:56:43,040
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Secretary, please.

1037
00:56:45,140 --> 00:56:46,620
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Thank you very much, Mr. Chair.

1038
00:56:46,860 --> 00:56:59,260
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Actually, itong meron pong consultation na dinadaanan po lahat yan, particularly kung meron na po silang existing na ECC, meron pong public consultation na dinadaanan yan.

1039
00:56:59,900 --> 00:57:11,600
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: And so, with the indulgence of the committee, Mr. Chair, we will submit all these documents to the Honorable Congresswoman after this hearing, Mr. Chair.

1040
00:57:11,900 --> 00:57:14,920
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Thank you. Please submit to Congresswoman Ismula.

1041
00:57:15,080 --> 00:57:16,140
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Thank you, Mr. Chair.

1042
00:57:16,160 --> 00:57:18,680
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: So, we will have a submission regarding Tampakan. Thank you.

1043
00:57:18,820 --> 00:57:19,820
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Thank you, Mr. Chair.

1044
00:57:19,860 --> 00:57:33,940
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Just put a note na lang po, Mr. Chair, sa ating ginoong sekretary na kadalasan po kasi ang nangyayari kaya siya na-re-renew ng hindi na nagkakaroon ng konsultasyon dahil nagkaroon na siya ng unang approval.

1045
00:57:34,400 --> 00:57:39,760
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: At nung nag-expire po siya, hindi po nila ito kinonsulta ang community ulit.

1046
00:57:39,760 --> 00:57:47,860
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Hindi po ba sa patakaran ng ating IPRA, kinakailangan po na magkonsulta po ulit kung ito ay nag-expire na.

1047
00:57:48,260 --> 00:57:49,620
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Dadako naman po ako.

1048
00:57:49,620 --> 00:58:05,880
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: On waste management, ano ang hakbang ng DNR para masiguro na ang LGU waste management contractors ay dumadaan sa mahigpit na vetting process at hindi nagiging instrumento ng conflict of interest ng mga lokal na opisyal?

1049
00:58:06,220 --> 00:58:08,700
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Meron po bang oversight ang DNR dito?

1050
00:58:10,680 --> 00:58:12,460
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Secretary, who will answer that question?

1051
00:58:13,780 --> 00:58:15,720
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Thank you very much, Mr. Chair, for the question.

1052
00:58:19,200 --> 00:58:21,520
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: As we know, under the law, RA

1053
00:58:21,520 --> 00:58:22,680
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: 9003.

1054
00:58:22,680 --> 00:58:28,940
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: The local government units have the responsibility when it comes to the waste management within their areas of jurisdiction.

1055
00:58:30,600 --> 00:58:42,460
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Ang responsibility naman po ng DNR is to provide technical assistance and to educate ang ating mga local government units, mga barangay,

1056
00:58:42,460 --> 00:58:51,260
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: on how we can assist in putting up the materials recovery facilities, in helping educate the people on segregation,

1057
00:58:51,260 --> 00:58:54,280
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: and other aspects of the law.

1058
00:58:54,660 --> 00:59:04,880
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: But pagdating po sa pag-engage ng private entity to do the waste management for the LGUs,

1059
00:59:05,580 --> 00:59:16,660
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: wala po kaming mandato to really look into the particular, alam po nila, Congressman Erice being also involved in the LGU.

1060
00:59:16,780 --> 00:59:19,360
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: So in that aspect, wala po kaming...

1061
00:59:19,360 --> 00:59:24,160
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Opinion or comment on this, Mr. Chair?

1062
00:59:24,960 --> 00:59:32,340
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Sakali po, Mr. Chair, na naintindihan ko po kung sinasabi po ng ating ginoong sekretary na wala silang mandato dito, no?

1063
00:59:32,340 --> 00:59:40,340
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Pero sakali po kayang may nai-report po sa kanila na ganito at pinapa-imbestigahan sa kanila, may action po ba silang ginagawa?

1064
00:59:41,120 --> 00:59:42,240
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Thank you, Mr. Chair.

1065
00:59:42,480 --> 00:59:43,660
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Opo, meron naman po.

1066
00:59:43,780 --> 00:59:48,480
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: We call the attention of the local government unit at nakipag-ugnayan po kami.

1067
00:59:48,540 --> 00:59:50,760
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Actually, with the local government units,

1068
00:59:50,760 --> 00:59:55,080
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: with Waste, tuloy-tuloy po ang coordination namin sa kanila, our regional offices,

1069
00:59:55,400 --> 00:59:56,480
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: continuously,

1070
00:59:56,940 --> 01:00:02,820
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: particularly the EMB, are in coordination with the local government units on solid waste management, Mr. Chair?

1071
01:00:04,440 --> 01:00:05,820
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Yes, Mr. Chair.

1072
01:00:05,920 --> 01:00:09,440
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: I have one more question regarding waste management.

1073
01:00:09,960 --> 01:00:14,940
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: If the waste management provider's contract is up for renewal,

1074
01:00:15,860 --> 01:00:21,560
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: will we have another consultation with the community regarding the performance of the contractor?

1075
01:00:23,960 --> 01:00:25,240
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Secretary, yes.

1076
01:00:26,340 --> 01:00:27,420
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Thank you, Mr. Chair.

1077
01:00:27,420 --> 01:00:35,580
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Actually, that exercise is purely with the LGU, Mr. Chair, and we are not part of that process, Mr. Chair.

1078
01:00:36,040 --> 01:00:44,360
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Mr. Chair, it looks like you're teaching because when we consulted, the LGU itself told us that it's the DENR.

1079
01:00:44,900 --> 01:00:46,000
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Anyway, I'm asking you...

1080
01:00:46,000 --> 01:00:46,740
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Which one, Secretary?

1081
01:00:46,940 --> 01:00:53,640
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: The statement of the Honorable Smula is that there has to be one primary...

1082
01:00:53,640 --> 01:00:55,060
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Thank you, Mr. Chair.

1083
01:00:55,060 --> 01:00:57,400
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: We are not involved

1084
01:00:57,400 --> 01:01:01,600
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: in the renewal of contracts of the private entities,

1085
01:01:01,600 --> 01:01:12,500
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: but it is within our mandate to monitor, for instance, sanitary landfills on compliance with the ECC conditions, Mr. Chair.

1086
01:01:13,680 --> 01:01:14,400
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Mr. Chair.

1087
01:01:14,500 --> 01:01:15,240
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Mr. Chairman.

1088
01:01:15,280 --> 01:01:16,640
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Yes, Mr. Congressman Egay.

1089
01:01:17,180 --> 01:01:18,780
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: There's local government autonomy.

1090
01:01:19,240 --> 01:01:22,840
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: So, the waste management providers are purely local.

1091
01:01:23,060 --> 01:01:25,460
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: If there's a complaint, just go to the DILG.

1092
01:01:25,640 --> 01:01:27,000
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: It's not DENR.

1093
01:01:27,080 --> 01:01:27,580
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Thank you.

1094
01:01:27,880 --> 01:01:28,620
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Maraming salamat ho, Mr. Chair.

1095
01:01:28,620 --> 01:01:29,620
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Thank you, Congressman Erice.

1096
01:01:29,960 --> 01:01:45,500
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Last but not least, for waste management, what does the DENR do to ensure that waste pickers have the right compensation and protection according to the Occupational Safety and Health Standards?

1097
01:01:45,840 --> 01:01:49,000
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: And how do contractors monitor compliance?

1098
01:01:50,160 --> 01:01:51,000
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Thank you, Mr. Chair.

1099
01:01:51,100 --> 01:01:55,360
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: If I may defer to Assistant Secretary Noreen Ran of Enforcement, Mr. Chair.

1100
01:01:55,360 --> 01:01:57,100
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Under Secretary Noreen Ran.

1101
01:01:57,140 --> 01:01:57,700
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Please proceed.

1102
01:01:58,150 --> 01:01:59,140
DENR Assistant Secretary Norlito A. Eneran: Thank you, Mr. Chair.

1103
01:02:00,060 --> 01:02:04,960
DENR Assistant Secretary Norlito A. Eneran: What we're doing when it comes to this, in fact, with the RA 9003,

1104
01:02:05,080 --> 01:02:09,000
DENR Assistant Secretary Norlito A. Eneran: it's prohibited for the settlers in our sanitary landfills.

1105
01:02:09,460 --> 01:02:10,160
DENR Assistant Secretary Norlito A. Eneran: It's prohibited.

1106
01:02:10,360 --> 01:02:16,100
DENR Assistant Secretary Norlito A. Eneran: So, the employment of the employees in the area,

1107
01:02:16,100 --> 01:02:19,620
DENR Assistant Secretary Norlito A. Eneran: there's no DENR mandate.

1108
01:02:19,700 --> 01:02:25,580
DENR Assistant Secretary Norlito A. Eneran: This is purely an operation of our provider and LGU.

1109
01:02:26,000 --> 01:02:27,120
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Okay.

1110
01:02:27,220 --> 01:02:32,640
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: I'll go to the wider discussion of forest governance and community rights.

1111
01:02:33,020 --> 01:02:41,640
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: The DENR announced 38 trillion pesos forest investments from 2027 to 2052,

1112
01:02:41,640 --> 01:02:46,460
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: which is expected to provide work and livelihood to rural communities.

1113
01:02:46,460 --> 01:02:55,260
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: In addition, the DENR released Department Administrative Order No. 2026-34

1114
01:02:55,260 --> 01:02:58,920
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Distribution of the Forest Management Bureau

1115
01:02:58,920 --> 01:03:05,420
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: of more than 1.18 million hectares of potential investment areas

1116
01:03:05,420 --> 01:03:11,040
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: through the Sustainable Forest Land Management Agreements.

1117
01:03:11,040 --> 01:03:13,480
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: With such a large investment,

1118
01:03:14,120 --> 01:03:26,000
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: I would like to know how much was allocated to monitoring SFMAs and forest investment portfolio packages in NEP 2027.

1119
01:03:26,960 --> 01:03:35,800
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Thank you very much Mr. Chair. I'd like to refer to the Forest Mansion Bureau Director Art Fadikella, Mr. Chair.

1120
01:03:37,880 --> 01:03:42,660
FMB Director Arturo E. Fadriquela: Good afternoon, Mr. President. Good afternoon, Mr. Chairman.

1121
01:03:43,540 --> 01:03:51,940
FMB Director Arturo E. Fadriquela: Regarding the announcement of our distinguished congressman in our investment area,

1122
01:03:51,940 --> 01:04:05,400
FMB Director Arturo E. Fadriquela: it is true that we are dealing with 1.18 million hectares of potential investment area.

1123
01:04:08,380 --> 01:04:20,820
FMB Director Arturo E. Fadriquela: We are offering this to investors and once we have the applications and we have provided the tenured instruments,

1124
01:04:21,940 --> 01:04:35,520
FMB Director Arturo E. Fadriquela: we are ready to ensure that they follow the regulations and the conditions provided by the DNR.

1125
01:04:35,660 --> 01:04:48,840
FMB Director Arturo E. Fadriquela: Now, we have been given three Sustainable Forest Management Agreements

1126
01:04:48,840 --> 01:04:52,880
FMB Director Arturo E. Fadriquela: according to the Department of Administrative Order that has been issued.

1127
01:04:52,880 --> 01:05:02,200
FMB Director Arturo E. Fadriquela: And when they implement the projects,

1128
01:05:02,400 --> 01:05:14,420
FMB Director Arturo E. Fadriquela: we will give them to the Department of Administrative Order, to our regional offices for monitoring of what they are doing.

1129
01:05:14,950 --> 01:05:23,760
FMB Director Arturo E. Fadriquela: So, we will give the funds when the projects are ready.

1130
01:05:25,440 --> 01:05:31,760
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Mr. Chair, thank you first to FMB Director Art Fadikella.

1131
01:05:32,650 --> 01:05:34,180
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Please proceed. Yes, we'll give you more time.

1132
01:05:34,180 --> 01:05:35,260
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Yes, Mr. Chair, this is the last time.

1133
01:05:35,260 --> 01:05:38,680
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: It looks like I didn't get the answer that I needed.

1134
01:05:38,680 --> 01:05:44,880
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: What I am asking is, if we have this kind of program,

1135
01:05:45,400 --> 01:05:50,600
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: what I just want to see is how much we have invested in NEP for 2027.

1136
01:05:50,860 --> 01:05:53,300
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Budget, how much is placed there?

1137
01:05:53,480 --> 01:05:59,560
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Mr. Chair, if I may defer to Usec Jonas Leones, who supervises the Forest Management Bureau.

1138
01:06:00,360 --> 01:06:01,120
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Usec Leones.

1139
01:06:01,500 --> 01:06:02,780
DENR Undersecretary Jonas R. Leones: Thank you, Mr. Chair.

1140
01:06:03,040 --> 01:06:04,360
DENR Undersecretary Jonas R. Leones: Just to respond

1141
01:06:04,360 --> 01:06:07,400
DENR Undersecretary Jonas R. Leones: to the question of the Honorable Congresswoman,

1142
01:06:07,400 --> 01:06:11,880
DENR Undersecretary Jonas R. Leones: since the program is still new,

1143
01:06:12,320 --> 01:06:18,160
DENR Undersecretary Jonas R. Leones: few of our, few have been applying for the SFLMA.

1144
01:06:18,680 --> 01:06:22,060
DENR Undersecretary Jonas R. Leones: But even then, just to inform the Honorable Congresswoman

1145
01:06:22,060 --> 01:06:28,420
DENR Undersecretary Jonas R. Leones: that we have already allocated for 2027 an amount of 60 million

1146
01:06:28,420 --> 01:06:34,600
DENR Undersecretary Jonas R. Leones: for monitoring, compliance monitoring of these tenure holders that we have awarded.

1147
01:06:34,860 --> 01:06:36,260
DENR Undersecretary Jonas R. Leones: Madam Congresswoman.

1148
01:06:36,340 --> 01:06:37,280
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: 60 million, right?

1149
01:06:37,460 --> 01:06:38,280
DENR Undersecretary Jonas R. Leones: 60 million.

1150
01:06:38,640 --> 01:06:39,040
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Yes.

1151
01:06:39,100 --> 01:06:41,240
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: That's the answer, Representative Ismula.

1152
01:06:41,400 --> 01:06:41,800
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Yes.

1153
01:06:41,800 --> 01:06:43,160
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Thank you very much, Mr. Chair.

1154
01:06:43,240 --> 01:06:45,720
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Thank you very much to our DNR.

1155
01:06:45,960 --> 01:06:46,600
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Thank you very much.

1156
01:06:46,600 --> 01:06:48,460
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Before I proceed to the next interpellator,

1157
01:06:48,660 --> 01:06:50,960
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: let me have an omnibus recognition.

