01:56:03,520 --> 01:56:05,540
Rep. Arlene "Kaka" J. Bag-ao: Hindi rin po namin alam ano pong mangyayari.

2085
01:56:05,540 --> 01:56:06,760
Rep. Arlene "Kaka" J. Bag-ao: Ano po ba?

2086
01:56:06,820 --> 01:56:10,160
Rep. Arlene "Kaka" J. Bag-ao: Asa po ba kami isasara ito dahil bonsai forest po siya.

2087
01:56:10,160 --> 01:56:14,180
Rep. Arlene "Kaka" J. Bag-ao: Tatlo lang po ang bonsai forest sa buong Pilipinas kasama ang Dinagat Islands.

2088
01:56:14,180 --> 01:56:18,280
Rep. Arlene "Kaka" J. Bag-ao: Pero hanggang ngayon may MPSA application po, Sec.

2089
01:56:18,280 --> 01:56:23,380
Rep. Arlene "Kaka" J. Bag-ao: At in fact, may declaration na ang DENR na sana po ay hindi matuloy ang mining dyan.

2090
01:56:24,240 --> 01:56:31,900
Rep. Arlene "Kaka" J. Bag-ao: Dahilan po, ang threat sa amin, araw-araw, at nagkaka-declare lang po ng aming LGU ng State of Calamity

2091
01:56:31,900 --> 01:56:37,120
Rep. Arlene "Kaka" J. Bag-ao: kasi 17,000 na po ang naapektuhan ng absence ng tubig.

2092
01:56:37,180 --> 01:56:42,120
Rep. Arlene "Kaka" J. Bag-ao: Kasi kung dito po ay baha ang issue, doon po ay wala po kaming tubig dahil sa sobrang init.

2093
01:56:42,120 --> 01:56:50,180
Rep. Arlene "Kaka" J. Bag-ao: At ang pinagbibintangan po kayo sa amin, na ang dahilan po ay dahil napuputol ang lahat ng puno sa aming mga bukid.

2094
01:56:50,180 --> 01:56:53,880
Rep. Arlene "Kaka" J. Bag-ao: Pero kung lack of education and information,

2095
01:56:54,280 --> 01:56:59,640
Rep. Arlene "Kaka" J. Bag-ao: wala po kaming makakausap kasi wala po kayong opisyal na pumupunta sa amin to monitor.

2096
01:56:59,840 --> 01:57:03,760
Rep. Arlene "Kaka" J. Bag-ao: Specifically, sir, can I ask that we talk about this?

2097
01:57:03,840 --> 01:57:07,640
Rep. Arlene "Kaka" J. Bag-ao: I will wait. I will not accuse you of anything yet.

2098
01:57:07,900 --> 01:57:13,300
Rep. Arlene "Kaka" J. Bag-ao: Pero can I ask lang po, una po, can somebody go there?

2099
01:57:13,300 --> 01:57:15,580
Rep. Arlene "Kaka" J. Bag-ao: And I can even accompany you, no?

2100
01:57:15,780 --> 01:57:22,800
Rep. Arlene "Kaka" J. Bag-ao: Can somebody go there to inform the people what is really the status of Hibusong Island and the East Coast mining?

2101
01:57:23,240 --> 01:57:31,140
Rep. Arlene "Kaka" J. Bag-ao: And please don't tell us, we know that already, that there is no pending operation permit that was given.

2102
01:57:31,500 --> 01:57:34,600
Rep. Arlene "Kaka" J. Bag-ao: Pero hindi naman ang threat ay nag-uumpisa kapag may permit po, di ba?

2103
01:57:35,240 --> 01:57:41,540
Rep. Arlene "Kaka" J. Bag-ao: Kahit po yung pananakot lang na hala bukas ay magsasara na kami, ay magbubukas na kami, ay threat na mismo.

2104
01:57:41,820 --> 01:57:44,160
Rep. Arlene "Kaka" J. Bag-ao: So, and that's the one. Can we go there?

2105
01:57:44,200 --> 01:57:52,600
Rep. Arlene "Kaka" J. Bag-ao: Second, can the ending of the process be a declaration of closure of mining operation?

2106
01:57:53,180 --> 01:57:59,460
Rep. Arlene "Kaka" J. Bag-ao: Dalawa lang po muna, isa-isa, para hindi tayo masyadong demanding naman, sir, no?

2107
01:57:59,600 --> 01:58:05,220
Rep. Arlene "Kaka" J. Bag-ao: Una po yung very small area. I think it's already less than 1,000 hectares na the area of Hibusong.

2108
01:58:05,880 --> 01:58:08,520
Rep. Arlene "Kaka" J. Bag-ao: Can we declare that area closed for mining?

2109
01:58:08,940 --> 01:58:16,820
Rep. Arlene "Kaka" J. Bag-ao: Pwede naman po, sir, hindi nyo nga pa-operate eh. Kahit may initial permit na kayo for East Coast.

2110
01:58:17,100 --> 01:58:20,720
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Thank you, Congresswoman Kaka. We'll let them answer.

2111
01:58:20,940 --> 01:58:21,760
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Two issues.

2112
01:58:22,800 --> 01:58:25,000
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Are you going to close that mining company?

2113
01:58:25,200 --> 01:58:28,420
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Second, who will go as early as possible to Dinagat Island?

2114
01:58:29,240 --> 01:58:29,640
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Please answer.

2115
01:58:30,080 --> 01:58:30,980
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Thank you, Mr. Chair.

2116
01:58:31,140 --> 01:58:33,580
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Usec. Fragada of Operations will answer, Mr. Chair.

2117
01:58:33,660 --> 01:58:34,460
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Thank you, Usec. Fragada.

2118
01:58:34,640 --> 01:58:35,360
DENR Undersecretary for Field Operations and Line Bureaus Joselin Marcus E. Fragada: Thank you, Mr. Chair.

2119
01:58:35,480 --> 01:58:36,780
DENR Undersecretary for Field Operations and Line Bureaus Joselin Marcus E. Fragada: To the good Congresswoman.

2120
01:58:36,880 --> 01:58:47,200
DENR Undersecretary for Field Operations and Line Bureaus Joselin Marcus E. Fragada: Yes, we committed, I committed to the good Congresswoman that we would go down and visit probably our head for enforcement or even myself to check out Dinagat Island.

2121
01:58:47,200 --> 01:58:49,220
DENR Undersecretary for Field Operations and Line Bureaus Joselin Marcus E. Fragada: To answer the question, yes.

2122
01:58:50,180 --> 01:58:52,340
DENR Undersecretary for Field Operations and Line Bureaus Joselin Marcus E. Fragada: I am aware of the bonsai forest.

2123
01:58:52,700 --> 01:58:57,220
DENR Undersecretary for Field Operations and Line Bureaus Joselin Marcus E. Fragada: I assure the good Congresswoman there will be no mining in that area, number one.

2124
01:58:57,220 --> 01:59:05,000
DENR Undersecretary for Field Operations and Line Bureaus Joselin Marcus E. Fragada: Number two, for that particular island, we apologize if there was an announcement made through social media.

2125
01:59:05,120 --> 01:59:14,400
DENR Undersecretary for Field Operations and Line Bureaus Joselin Marcus E. Fragada: But officially, I will make sure that the region comes up with a proper statement regarding the notice to the public.

2126
01:59:14,660 --> 01:59:21,600
DENR Undersecretary for Field Operations and Line Bureaus Joselin Marcus E. Fragada: But to further her request, we're in the process of cleansing mining claims as well.

2127
01:59:21,780 --> 01:59:22,460
DENR Undersecretary for Field Operations and Line Bureaus Joselin Marcus E. Fragada: So I reassure...

2128
01:59:23,000 --> 01:59:35,800
DENR Undersecretary for Field Operations and Line Bureaus Joselin Marcus E. Fragada: I assure the good Congresswoman that we will take a look at the claims in the area and probably through the PENRO, we can assign someone specifically to address monitoring of mining areas, ma'am, para makita rin po natin kung ano nangyari.

2129
01:59:35,940 --> 01:59:38,260
DENR Undersecretary for Field Operations and Line Bureaus Joselin Marcus E. Fragada: So I hope that answers your question.

2130
01:59:38,360 --> 01:59:41,580
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Yes, eventually, we can move already for the...

2131
01:59:42,680 --> 01:59:43,700
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: There's no categorical answer.

2132
01:59:43,840 --> 01:59:44,980
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Are you going to close it or not?

2133
01:59:45,620 --> 01:59:52,580
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: It's very clear that there is really much reason to declare the closure of any mining in that island.

2134
01:59:53,020 --> 01:59:53,760
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Yes, Mr. Chair.

2135
01:59:53,900 --> 01:59:55,680
DENR Undersecretary for Field Operations and Line Bureaus Joselin Marcus E. Fragada: Mr. Chair, kung meron po talaga operations, yes.

2136
01:59:56,360 --> 01:59:58,220
DENR Undersecretary for Field Operations and Line Bureaus Joselin Marcus E. Fragada: Specifically po doon sa area na yun.

2137
01:59:58,340 --> 02:00:02,640
Rep. Arlene "Kaka" J. Bag-ao: So you're not going to extend any mining claim or approve it?

2138
02:00:03,200 --> 02:00:07,000
DENR Undersecretary for Field Operations and Line Bureaus Joselin Marcus E. Fragada: Sir, doon po sa area na binabang-, Mr. Chair, na binabanggit ni Congresswoman,

2139
02:00:07,240 --> 02:00:11,480
DENR Undersecretary for Field Operations and Line Bureaus Joselin Marcus E. Fragada: wala po talagang existing na ano na doon.

2140
02:00:11,780 --> 02:00:18,540
DENR Undersecretary for Field Operations and Line Bureaus Joselin Marcus E. Fragada: So that's why I can commit to her that after check-in, we can automatically close if need be.

2141
02:00:18,780 --> 02:00:19,840
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Thank you very much.

2142
02:00:19,960 --> 02:00:21,420
