Rep. Elmer V. Catulpos: Okay, thank you, ma'am. Thank you, Mr. Chair. Another thing, sa Jensen, nung tumama yung magnitude 7.8 na lindol,

5938
05:31:52,560 --> 05:31:57,260
Rep. Elmer V. Catulpos: napagalaman namin na a year before nangyari yun,

5939
05:31:57,260 --> 05:32:07,160
Rep. Elmer V. Catulpos: nagsumite na ng report si PHIVOLCS sa LGU na kung saan merong 38% sa barangay ng GenSan may liquefaction.

5940
05:32:08,880 --> 05:33:02,640
Rep. Elmer V. Catulpos: Yung concern ko sa MGB, yung sa geohazard mapping, paano siya ma-merge or ma-integrate yung liquefaction? Kasi with our experience, pag nagbigay yung PHIVOLCS doon sa LGU, hindi nami-merge yung data sa geohazard mapping nila. Hindi naka-layer. So, magkaiba yung data na natatanggap at saka yung sa geohazard mapping. Ngayon, paano siya makaka-comply yung mga bagong building permits at saka yung zoning ng CLUP? Dadalawa yung basis nila. Mr. Secretary.

5941
05:33:03,960 --> 05:33:05,820
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: Thank you very much, Mr. Chair.

5942
05:33:05,820 --> 05:33:10,280
DENR Acting Secretary Juan Miguel T. Cuna: We'd like to defer to Dr. Karlo. The assistant director of MGB.

5943
05:33:11,460 --> 05:33:33,840
MGB Assistant Director Karlo L. Queaño: Thank you, Secretary. I'd like to respond. As a geologist, we're implementing the Department Administrative Order 2000-28 in which all infrastructures, whether government or private, should conduct an engineering, geological, and geo-hazard assessment as an additional requirement for the issuance of the ECC.

5944
05:33:34,160 --> 05:33:43,700
MGB Assistant Director Karlo L. Queaño: So, essentially, before you construct a building, you should know the physical conditions, if it's liquefaction-prone, if it's flood-prone, or maybe if it's landslide-prone.

5945
05:33:43,780 --> 05:34:08,340
MGB Assistant Director Karlo L. Queaño: So, basically, you map out all of these geo-hazards. So, it's not just simply superimposing the liquefaction because liquefaction and volcanic-related hazards are the mandates of the Philippine Institute of Volcanology. But in the same way, identifying the faults, and that's also perform the fevals. But on the side of the MGB, DNR, that's flooding and landslide, as well as what we call the karst, and to a certain extent, coast.

5946
05:34:08,660 --> 05:34:16,920
MGB Assistant Director Karlo L. Queaño: But regardless of the mandate, it is important in the DNR admissive order that all of these hazards are looked into by the private entity.

5947
05:34:17,240 --> 05:34:37,940
MGB Assistant Director Karlo L. Queaño: So, the process is the private entity would hire a private geologist to produce an engineering, geological, and geo-hazard assessment, after which the DNR MGB would review that document as to whether the document is able to address this hazard and design a particular infrastructure according to the hazard.

5948
05:34:38,080 --> 05:34:40,840
MGB Assistant Director Karlo L. Queaño: So, it's not just simply mitigating, but also adapting the structure.

5949
05:34:40,840 --> 05:34:44,060
Rep. Elmer V. Catulpos: Okay. Mr. Chair, yung concern lang,

5950
05:34:44,060 --> 05:34:49,180
Rep. Elmer V. Catulpos: yung sa geo-hazard mapping ba ng DNR, kasama na ang liquefaction doon?

5951
05:34:49,180 --> 05:34:51,440
Rep. Elmer V. Catulpos: Hindi. Feebox yun?

5952
05:34:51,640 --> 05:34:56,000
MGB Assistant Director Karlo L. Queaño: Yes po. That's why po, in the geo-risk hazards hunter,

5953
05:34:56,000 --> 05:35:01,160
MGB Assistant Director Karlo L. Queaño: these maps are integrated so that the end user would be able to make use of all of these maps po.

5954
05:35:01,160 --> 05:35:33,040
Rep. Elmer V. Catulpos: Hindi kasi yung concern namin, nalimbawa sa DPWH, yung sabi ng DPWH, hindi magkakaroon, nang future, kailangan may concordance ng DNR, yung mga future projects, especially related to flood control. Pero kung hindi nakasama yung liquefaction map doon sa basis ni DNR, possible pa rin na may mangyayaring masama kung sakaling may liquefaction na hindi siya na-factor in doon.

5955
05:35:33,620 --> 05:35:40,740
MGB Assistant Director Karlo L. Queaño: Tama po yan. That's why po, importante po sa isang building, or whatever infrastructure that these hazards are integrated,

5956
05:35:41,160 --> 05:35:46,560
MGB Assistant Director Karlo L. Queaño: unfortunately po for Gensan, it is underlain, a large portion of it is underlain by Lahar.

5957
05:35:46,820 --> 05:35:50,700
MGB Assistant Director Karlo L. Queaño: That's the reason why kapag naglindolo, matindi po yung ground shaking po niya.

5958
05:35:50,940 --> 05:35:57,180
MGB Assistant Director Karlo L. Queaño: And also, liquefaction is one of those, what you call these consequences of strong ground shaking.

5959
05:35:57,180 --> 05:36:02,700
MGB Assistant Director Karlo L. Queaño: That's why po, sa mga ganyang klaseng mga lugar, importante yung na-integrate yan sa design.

5960
05:36:02,980 --> 05:36:08,400
MGB Assistant Director Karlo L. Queaño: I mean to say, yung liquefiable, for example, na layer, ay bina-bypass po ng foundation ng isang building mo.

5961
05:36:08,500 --> 05:36:19,800
MGB Assistant Director Karlo L. Queaño: But I believe po, because of the DNR business order, that is actually a requirement for all these private entities to integrate all of these hazards before implementing that project po.

5962
05:36:20,180 --> 05:36:26,120
Rep. Elmer V. Catulpos: Mr. Chair, yung concern ko, Mr. Chair, kung may way ba na ma-merge yung data na yan,

5963
05:36:30,860 --> 05:36:46,100
Rep. Elmer V. Catulpos: DNR, ma-merge yung data na yan para pag nagbigay ng certification or concurrency DNR, kasama na yun, na-consider na yung ano, kasama yung data, nang liquefaction.

5964
05:36:46,320 --> 05:36:47,280
MGB Assistant Director Karlo L. Queaño: May I reply po?

5965
05:36:47,500 --> 05:36:55,180
MGB Assistant Director Karlo L. Queaño: Actually po, the municipalities at lahat po ng mga provincial, they can actually superimpose all of these maps.

5966
05:36:55,180 --> 05:36:58,160
MGB Assistant Director Karlo L. Queaño: Dahil lang po yan ay available po nga po sa Hazards Hunter.

5967
05:36:58,480 --> 05:37:08,380
MGB Assistant Director Karlo L. Queaño: But of course, on the part of the DNR MGB, we are also offer our assistance to review all of the CLUP that also integrates this kind of hazard.

5968
05:37:08,500 --> 05:37:16,460
MGB Assistant Director Karlo L. Queaño: So as to be able to all these local governments to understand, and how to actually make use of those maps in the context of their land use plans.

5969
05:37:17,580 --> 05:37:20,760
Rep. Elmer V. Catulpos: Okay, that's all, Mr. Chair. Thank you.

5970
05:37:21,000 --> 05:37:21,880
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Thank you very much.

